WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.171
Ta-da!

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.841
Hi, it's N-ko!

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:11.578
This week's The N-ko Show has started!

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.580
It's Friday already.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.982
A week goes by so quickly.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.550
By the way,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.989
the tea swiss roll I had the other day was absolutely delicious.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:27.894
It was sold at a pastry shop near my home, and I bought a piece of it.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.796
It was so delicious

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.098
that I want to buy and eat

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.267
a whole roll the next time.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.502
Well then,

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.071
let's start The N-ko Show!

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.741
Weekly Favorites!

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:49.149
I will share my recommendations based on my personal picks again.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.484
This week's theme is this.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.254
Anime to watch when you want to cry.

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.289
When you want to vent about stress

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.924
or want some stimulation,

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:01.261
perhaps some people might want to watch touching anime.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.830
I would like to recommend you

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.032
touching anime that make you cry.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.268
They're anime that strongly stimulate your mind,

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:12.572
which will make you cry to reset your emotions.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.841
Let me share them with you.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.377
Touching anime that make you cry.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.045
Here is the first one.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:23.717
ANOHANA: THE FLOWER WE SAW THAT DAY.

00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:27.587
It's an anime that must be included in this theme.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.889
Please don't say it's stereotyped.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.992
Some of you may have only heard of the name

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.261
but haven't watched it yet.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.665
Or maybe you've seen the scene of a girl crying,

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:42.135
or you know the song "Secret Base," which is used in the anime.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:45.338
If you think any of the above is you,

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.007
then go watch it at once.

00:01:47.007 --> 00:01:48.575
With romance as its axis,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:51.277
answers to various doubts are revealed,

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.347
and there's a series of touching moments in the anime.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.849
In the final episode,

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.651
there's a point that intensely makes you cry.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.588
The opening song, "Aoi Shiori,"

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:04.758
was also written for this anime.

00:02:04.758 --> 00:02:07.494
The melody is clear and sad,

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:12.232
and the lyrics reflect the feelings of the characters.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.566
It's really wonderful.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.735
After you watch the whole anime,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.470
just listening to this song

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.205
is enough to make you cry.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:23.710
The next touching anime I'll recommend that makes you cry is this.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.812
VIOLET EVERGARDEN.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.715
Please don't say this is stereotyped too.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:34.087
This anime is just a continuous storm of touching moments.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.556
The growth of its protagonist, Violet,

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:40.226
and heart-warming episodes of people around her are depicted,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.897
expressing the love of people in various forms.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.900
They make your eyes and heart cry.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.703
After you finish watching this anime,

00:02:49.703 --> 00:02:51.538
you'll realize again

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:55.208
that telling people how you feel, being kind, and loving people

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:59.913
are important in their own unique ways.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:04.184
It has a touching story and animation you're going to love,

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:08.722
so you're going to be satisfied and cry for sure.

00:03:08.722 --> 00:03:12.158
Next, I'll recommend anime that stimulate your mind

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:16.129
and make you cry with mixed feelings.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.464
Here's the first one.

00:03:17.464 --> 00:03:19.866
IN THIS CORNER OF THE WORLD.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:23.169
During the World War, even when she had various troubles,

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.238
no matter how harsh the situation was,

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.007
by coming up with new ideas

00:03:27.007 --> 00:03:29.175
and making effort on her way of life,

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.011
Suzu lives with a positive attitude.

00:03:31.011 --> 00:03:35.148
It touches your heart and makes you cry.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:39.085
It's easy to put yourself in protagonist Suzu's shoes.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:44.524
You'll agree with Suzu's words and empathize with her when you watch it.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.394
This is also the anime's characteristic.

00:03:47.394 --> 00:03:51.231
Also, when I think about many people in this world

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.767
having actually experienced those things,

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:55.635
it makes me very sad.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:59.773
"I should take the message of this anime seriously,"

00:03:59.773 --> 00:04:01.241
I think.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:07.247
This anime makes your various emotions gush out and makes you cry.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.015
Next, it's this anime.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.717
A SILENT VOICE.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:15.455
There are many anime that use romance with people with a disablity as a theme,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.191
but this anime specifically describes

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:22.696
the feelings of the person with a disability and the people around her.

00:04:22.696 --> 00:04:26.433
It's very realistic.

00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:29.602
There are heartbreaking scenes everywhere.

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:33.573
Protagonist Shoya Ishida's thoughts and actions

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:36.843
make you ponder all kinds of things.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:41.815
Empathizing with the characters and pondering things

00:04:41.815 --> 00:04:43.516
will make your heart ache.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:47.087
There's sadness, pain, worry, and relief.

00:04:47.087 --> 00:04:51.458
This anime really will stir your heart.

00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:54.561
To be honest, even when you don't want to cry,

00:04:54.561 --> 00:04:57.597
you should watch this anime at least once.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.366
All of the anime I've introduced today

00:04:59.366 --> 00:05:01.468
will make you cry very hard,

00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:05.405
so please watch them when you want to feel refreshed.

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:08.308
That's it for Weekly Favorites.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.578
N-ko's Monologue.

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:15.815
This part has no specific theme.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:18.651
I'm just going to say what I think,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.620
and it's very light-hearted.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.657
Like things I've been thinking of and doing lately.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:28.061
Or I'll talk about people I'm a big fan of.

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:31.297
It's a segment where we just talk freely.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.298
This time,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:36.836
I'm going to talk to you about the life hack I found.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:40.707
We've been staying home a lot since last year, right?

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:47.080
I also work from home and just eat at home every day,

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.848
so when I'm busy with work

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.384
or when I don't want to prepare a meal,

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:56.523
I often just eat ready-made meals.

00:05:56.523 --> 00:06:00.994
There have been times I ate ready-made meals since before this,

00:06:00.994 --> 00:06:02.962
so I know various kinds of them.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:07.834
But there are many high-quality ones available lately.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.503
Among them,

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:15.375
I finally found the best combination of ready-made meals.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:20.246
That is retort-pouch curry on oatmeal.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:23.650
Oatmeal is healthy and chewy.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:28.388
It goes very well with some spicy curry.

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:31.591
Even if you have no rice, if you have some oatmeal,

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.993
you can make curry rice!

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:38.031
I don't know if I can call it curry "rice" though.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:43.169
I wanted to tell someone about this combination so much that I felt restless.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:44.971
So I feel great that I've said it.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.973
Please do try it yourself!

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.976
That's it for N-ko's Monologue.

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:53.413
N-ko's Q &amp; A Section!

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:57.450
I will answer your questions again this week.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.519
Let's start.

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.454
This is the first question.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:03.823
Why are you a sheep?

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:06.326
Why are you a human being?

00:07:07.027 --> 00:07:09.829
If you choose between two ninja anime,

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:13.833
do you like NINTAMA RANTARO or NARUTO more?

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.802
It's NARUTO!

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:17.771
Your favorite video game?

00:07:17.771 --> 00:07:20.674
Apex Legends. I want to play in the tournament!

00:07:20.674 --> 00:07:25.412
Do you feel any difference between American and Japanese cultures?

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:30.850
I think everything in America is big.

00:07:31.351 --> 00:07:33.520
What's your favorite sweet?

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:34.788
Pudding!

00:07:34.788 --> 00:07:37.357
Thank you for your questions.

00:07:37.357 --> 00:07:41.728
I'm still waiting for you to send me your questions!

00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:44.898
That's it for N-ko's Q &amp; A.

00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:51.438
The N-ko Show! It's now time to say goodbye.

00:07:51.438 --> 00:07:55.241
I've introduced many touching anime today,

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:59.212
so please remember to keep yourself hydrated!

00:07:59.212 --> 00:08:03.483
I'm going to explore the possibilities of cream stew and oatmeal

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.485
before next week.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:09.489
Let's meet again next time.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.990
See you!

